# ─── Environment + Secrets ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Never commit a real .env. The reference copy lives in .env.example.
# Any file with .env in the name (e.g. db.env, prod.env) is also
# excluded by the wildcard below.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.env
*.secret
*.secrets
secrets.*
secrets/

# TLS and key material — anything a newcomer might accidentally
# generate inside the repo for local testing.
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.cer
*.p12
*.pfx
*.der
*.jks

# Databases and data dumps
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
*.dump

# ─── Local uploads and data volumes ───────────────────────────────────
/data/
uploads/
backend/uploads/

# ─── Generic cache ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.cache/

# ─── Tool-specific local state ────────────────────────────────────────
# Claude Code session data, Playwright debugging artifacts,
# and the local design-system scratch directory.
.claude/
.playwright-mcp/
.interface-design/

# Loose competitor-analysis screenshots and debug images that
# sometimes accumulate in the repo root during active development.
# Keep them out of the public repo entirely.
